WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Last time, a cell recycled purines because building them is costly.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.460
A dividing cell must copy all its DNA, so it needs building blocks fast.

3
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.680
One drug is shaped almost like the vitamin folate.

4
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.260
How can a vitamin look-alike starve that copying?

5
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:24.493
But DNA needs deoxy building blocks.

6
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:30.513
In a dividing cell, most new ones come through one gateway, ribonucleotide

7
00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:33.553
reductase, which reduces ribonucleotides.

8
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.473
Its activity is tied tightly to cell division.

9
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:40.403
Thymine needs one more step.

10
00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:46.023
Thymidylate synthase adds a carbon, carried by a folate, to dUMP.

11
00:00:47.243 --> 00:00:52.243
That makes thymidylate, dTMP, and leaves the folate as dihydrofolate.

12
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:58.177
Dihydrofolate reductase, DHFR, turns it back into THF.

13
00:00:59.397 --> 00:01:01.397
Only then can it carry another carbon.

14
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:05.797
The same carrier supplies two carbons of the purine ring.

15
00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:10.297
So one folate loop feeds both thymidylate and purines.

16
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:16.227
Here is the rule. An enzyme accepts what has the right shape.

17
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:22.227
A counterfeit that fits the lock well enough to turn it, or jam it, is a medicine,

18
00:01:22.687 --> 00:01:23.867
an antimetabolite.

19
00:01:25.007 --> 00:01:29.487
The dividing cell is the most exposed, because it needs nucleotides fastest.

20
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:36.867
Methotrexate mimics folate and jams DHFR, the enzyme that recycles the carrier.

21
00:01:38.087 --> 00:01:41.267
What runs short: thymidylate, the purine ring, or both?

22
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:53.183
Both. With DHFR jammed, THF is not regenerated.

23
00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:58.363
Thymidylate and the purine ring are both starved of their folate carbons.

24
00:01:59.523 --> 00:02:03.423
The cell runs short of the dTMP it needs to copy its DNA.

25
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.087
5-fluorouracil mimics uracil.

26
00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:13.287
Inside the cell it becomes FdUMP, which traps thymidylate synthase itself.

27
00:02:14.527 --> 00:02:17.487
A different lock, the same shortage of dTMP.

28
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:23.237
6-mercaptopurine, a fake purine, enters through the recycle door.

29
00:02:25.057 --> 00:02:29.677
HGPRT, the recycling enzyme, turns it into counterfeit nucleotides.

30
00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.477
These shut down purine building.

31
00:02:33.857 --> 00:02:38.617
Once built into DNA, they damage the leukemia cells that took up the drug.

32
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.990
So each of these drugs is almost right.

33
00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.650
Each fools an enzyme on the road to DNA.

34
00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:51.910
A dividing cell needs that road most, though fast-dividing normal tissues are hit

35
00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:52.190
too.
